msgid "3. Upload the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:100
msgid "Open the ``08-Bluetooth_remote_relay.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_esp01\\bluetooth\\08-Bluetooth_remote_relay``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:106
msgid "After selecting the correct board and port, click the **Upload** button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:108
msgid "Open the Serial monitor(set baudrate to **9600**) to view debug messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:111
msgid "4. App and Bluetooth module Connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:113
msgid "Ensure that the application created earlier is installed on your smartphone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:115
msgid "Initially, turn on **Bluetooth** on your smartphone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:121
msgid "Navigate to the **Bluetooth settings** on your smartphone and look for names like **JDY-31-SPP**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:127
msgid "After clicking it, agree to the **Pair** request in the pop-up window. If prompted for a pairing code, please enter \"1234\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:133
msgid "Now open the newly installed **Remote Relay** APP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:139
msgid "In the APP, click on **Connect** button to establish a connection between the APP and Bluetooth module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:145
msgid "This page displays a list of all paired Bluetooth devices. Choose the ``xx.xx.xx.xx.xx.xx JDY-31-SPP`` option from the list. The name of each device is listed next to its MAC address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:151
msgid "If you don't see any devices on the page shown above, it could be because this app is not authorized to scan for nearby devices. In such a case, you will need to adjust the settings manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:153
msgid "To access the **APP Info** page, long-press the app icon and select it. Alternatively, if you have another method to reach this page, use that instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:159
msgid "Navigate to the **Permissions** page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:165
msgid "To enable the APP to scan for nearby devices, go to **Nearby devices** and select **Always**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:171
msgid "Now, restart the APP and repeat steps 5 and 6 to successfully connect to Bluetooth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:173
msgid "After a successful connection, you will be redirected to the main page. Click the \"ON\" or \"OFF\" button to turn on or off the relay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:176
msgid "When the MAC address of Bluetooth contains \"1\", the relay will be turned on and then quickly turned off after the first successful Bluetooth connection. Because when the Bluetooth is connected, the MAC address will be sent to Arduino. Arduino detects \"1\" and then opens the relay. After Bluetooth initialization, the app sends 0 to Arduino via Bluetooth to ensure that the initial state of the relay is closed after connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:183
msgid "5. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:185
msgid "**Library and Global Variable Initialization**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:197
msgid "This segment includes the ``SoftwareSerial`` library and sets up the global variables. Pins 3 and 4 are defined for transmitting and receiving data with the Bluetooth module, respectively. Additionally, the relay module is connected to pin 8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:199
msgid "**setup() Function**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:209
msgid "It initiates the Serial monitor and Bluetooth module communication at a baud rate of 9600. It also sets the ``relayPin`` as an OUTPUT pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:211
msgid "**loop() Function**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/13-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:230
msgid "The ``loop()`` function runs continuously. It checks if there's a message received from the Bluetooth module. If a message is received, it reads the character. Depending on the character ('1' or '0'), it either turns the relay on or off and sends a confirmation message (\"On\" or \"Off\") to the Serial monitor."
msgstr ""
